Optimal Solution - Sliding window with frequency tracking to find the smallest substring containing all characters of t.
                   Maintain a required character counter and shrink the window only when all characters are satisfied.

class Solution {
    public String minWindow(String s, String t) {
        // Length of main string
        int n = s.length();
        // If target string is longer than s, impossible
        if (t.length() > n) return "";
        // Frequency map storing required characters from t
        Map<Character, Integer> map = new HashMap<>();
        // Fill frequency map
        for (char ch : t.toCharArray()) {
            map.put(ch, map.getOrDefault(ch, 0) + 1);
        }
        // Total number of characters still required
        int reqCnt = t.length();
        // Sliding window pointers
        int i = 0, j = 0;
        // Track minimum window size found
        int winSize = Integer.MAX_VALUE;
        // Track starting index of best window
        int start_i = 0;
        // Expand window using j
        while (j < n) {
            char ch = s.charAt(j);
            // If character is part of target
            if (map.containsKey(ch)) {
                // If still needed, reduce required count
                if (map.get(ch) > 0) {
                    reqCnt--;
                }
                // Decrease frequency (can go negative if extra)
                map.put(ch, map.get(ch) - 1);
            }
            // When we have a valid window
            while (reqCnt == 0) {
                int curSize = j - i + 1;
                // Update minimum window
                if (curSize < winSize) {
                    winSize = curSize;
                    start_i = i;
                }
                // Try to shrink window from left
                char leftChar = s.charAt(i);
                if (map.containsKey(leftChar)) {
                    // Restore frequency
                    map.put(leftChar, map.get(leftChar) + 1);
                    // If this character becomes needed again
                    if (map.get(leftChar) > 0) {
                        reqCnt++;
                    }
                }
                i++; // Move left pointer
            }
            j++; // Expand right pointer
        }
        // Return result
        return winSize == Integer.MAX_VALUE
                ? ""
                : s.substring(start_i, start_i + winSize);
    }
}

Time Complexity :- O(N).
Space Complexity :- O(K). size of the window.
